{#
  Shared macro: one `- schema: IdMap` outputs: entry, generated from a
  `parameters`-shaped list (each row: `id`, `external` -- a string, or a
  list of strings for a one-internal/many-externals mapping). Import into a
  pattern.yaml with:

      {% import '_partials/idmap_from_parameters.yaml.j2' as idmap %}
      ...
      outputs:
      - schema: TimeSeriesImportRun
        ...
{{ idmap.emit(output_path='IdMapFiles/.../IdImportX.xml', parameters=parameters) }}

  Centralizes the block already hand-duplicated across gfs/gribfilter,
  gfs/ensemble, nwp_grid_ecmwf_ifs, import_era5, import_cyclone_jtwc -- so
  the idMap a pattern emits can never drift from the `parameters` it
  actually declares (each row is the single source of truth for both).
  The `- schema: IdMap` line below is emitted at column 0 so it lines up as
  a sibling list item alongside the pattern's other `outputs:` entries; the
  macro call itself must also sit at column 0 in the calling pattern.yaml.

  A row with no `external` (e.g. a hand-authored blueprint override that
  predates this field, or a genuinely novel id a configurator added without
  idMap coverage) is skipped, not a hard failure -- same as today's
  behaviour for an id the idMap never mapped. Silently claiming coverage
  that isn't there would be worse; crashing the whole build over one
  under-specified row would be disproportionate. Use `p.get(...)`
  throughout (never `p.external`), which returns None for a missing key
  instead of raising under the StrictUndefined render pass.

  If NO row has an `external`, the macro emits nothing at all (not even
  the `- schema: IdMap` list item) -- an idMap with zero mappings is
  itself invalid (FEWS requires at least one), so there is no valid empty
  file to produce; better to omit the output than emit one guaranteed to
  fail validation.
#}
{%- macro emit(output_path, parameters, one_to_one=none) -%}
{%- set rows = [] %}
{%- for p in parameters %}
{%- set ext_value = p.get('external') %}
{%- set externals = [] if not ext_value else ([ext_value] if ext_value is string else ext_value) %}
{%- for ext in externals %}
{%- if rows.append({'internal': p.id, 'external': ext}) %}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if rows %}
- schema: IdMap
  output: {{ output_path }}
  data:
    version: '1.1'
    parameter:
{% for row in rows %}
    - internal: {{ row.internal }}
      external: '{{ row.external }}'
{% endfor %}
{% if one_to_one is not none %}
    enableOneToOneMapping: {{ 'true' if one_to_one else 'false' }}
{% endif %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
